WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:01.123
- Thank you very much.

00:00:01.123 --> 00:00:02.650
- You're here in person this time.

00:00:02.650 --> 00:00:03.490
- I'm here in person this time.

00:00:03.490 --> 00:00:04.323
- I know, I like it.

00:00:04.323 --> 00:00:05.156
- That's wonderful.

00:00:05.156 --> 00:00:05.989
- I will say though,

00:00:05.989 --> 00:00:06.822
I was very jealous of your trip

00:00:06.822 --> 00:00:08.170
that you were taking all
the pictures I loved.

00:00:08.170 --> 00:00:09.950
That was like my favorite Zoom.

00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:11.380
Like that board that you
showed us all the pictures,

00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:12.604
it was so cool.

00:00:12.604 --> 00:00:13.437
- It was fun, I like to travel.

00:00:13.437 --> 00:00:14.670
I like to get out in the world when I can,

00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:15.640
when I'm not in production.

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:17.091
- You do like to travel.

00:00:17.091 --> 00:00:17.924
- Yeah.

00:00:17.924 --> 00:00:18.757
- I was gonna wait later in the interview,

00:00:18.757 --> 00:00:20.907
but I heard that you
did even more traveling-

00:00:20.907 --> 00:00:21.740
- Oh man.

00:00:21.740 --> 00:00:22.573
- after you wrapped the last production.

00:00:22.573 --> 00:00:23.406
You go everywhere.

00:00:23.406 --> 00:00:24.310
- I did. I went everywhere.

00:00:24.310 --> 00:00:25.270
God, where do I start?

00:00:25.270 --> 00:00:27.310
I went to Portland to
go surprise my sister

00:00:27.310 --> 00:00:28.420
for her birthday.

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:30.131
- Oh I know Oregon, that's beautiful.

00:00:30.131 --> 00:00:31.240
- Then I flew to Indianapolis

00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:32.960
to go wave the green flag at The Indy 500.

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:34.053
- Oh, I've done Indy 500. That's fun.

00:00:34.053 --> 00:00:35.040
- It's fun.
- Yeah, yeah.

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:36.167
- One of my buddies, Connor
Daly's a racing driver

00:00:36.167 --> 00:00:37.120
- Oh wow.

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:37.953
and he was like, "Do
you want to come out?"

00:00:37.953 --> 00:00:38.960
- And I'm like, "Yeah, cool, great.

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:39.906
I'm not working so let's do it"

00:00:39.906 --> 00:00:40.739
- Yeah.

00:00:40.739 --> 00:00:41.572
- God, I was everywhere.

00:00:41.572 --> 00:00:42.405
I was at Fort Bragg doing some work

00:00:42.405 --> 00:00:43.238
- Oh, that's cool.

00:00:43.238 --> 00:00:44.920
- with special forces teams there.

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:46.840
I went to Switzerland
to go visit a friend,

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:48.840
went to Vancouver to visit another friend.

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:50.978
I took two weeks in my camper
- Wow.

00:00:50.978 --> 00:00:52.510
- around on the national parks,

00:00:52.510 --> 00:00:54.984
in like Yosemite and Utah.

00:00:54.984 --> 00:00:56.450
- Are you always by yourself?
- No.

00:00:56.450 --> 00:00:58.120
- Like, do you ever get lost?

00:00:58.120 --> 00:00:59.203
- There's a few U turns.

00:00:59.203 --> 00:01:00.340
(laughs)

00:01:00.340 --> 00:01:02.170
There's always a couple
U turns that happen

00:01:02.170 --> 00:01:03.648
within a trip or whatnot.

00:01:03.648 --> 00:01:04.481
- Yeah.

00:01:04.481 --> 00:01:05.330
- But I like to wander.

00:01:05.330 --> 00:01:07.100
I just like to wander around and sometimes

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:08.960
I'm with friends and
sometimes I'm by myself.

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:11.218
But if I'm just kinda
seeing something new-

00:01:11.218 --> 00:01:12.051
- Yeah.

00:01:12.051 --> 00:01:13.447
- I'm seeing something new,
then I think, you know,

00:01:13.447 --> 00:01:14.931
that's the way to go.

00:01:14.931 --> 00:01:15.764
- I mean, that's beautiful.

00:01:15.764 --> 00:01:16.597
- Oh Yeah.

00:01:16.597 --> 00:01:17.430
- Where are you there?

00:01:17.430 --> 00:01:18.430
- That is in Switzerland.

00:01:18.430 --> 00:01:19.263
- I love Switzerland.

00:01:19.263 --> 00:01:22.260
- That is, yeah, so that's
the real Matterhorn.

00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:24.360
I mean, of course growing
up in Orange County,

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:26.030
California at Disneyland.

00:01:26.030 --> 00:01:27.020
- You did arrive, yes.

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:28.880
- Yeah. You have the Matterhorn
and there's the fake one.

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:29.880
That's the real one.

00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:30.920
- That's so cool.

00:01:30.920 --> 00:01:31.753
- Yeah.

00:01:31.753 --> 00:01:33.030
- I feel like you need a traveling show

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:33.987
called "This is Me."

00:01:33.987 --> 00:01:34.820
"(laughs)

00:01:34.820 --> 00:01:35.653
- Something like that.

00:01:35.653 --> 00:01:37.087
It's the play of the plan of "This is Us."

00:01:37.087 --> 00:01:37.920
- Maybe, maybe.

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:39.530
- I'm just saying, you love traveling

00:01:39.530 --> 00:01:41.310
and people don't generally get to go see

00:01:41.310 --> 00:01:42.720
all that kind of stuff and it's awesome.

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:43.553
- I think if anything,

00:01:43.553 --> 00:01:44.950
hopefully me being out in the world

00:01:44.950 --> 00:01:46.167
inspires somebody else to say,

00:01:46.167 --> 00:01:47.580
"Oh, I wanna go there. I wanna do this.

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:48.413
- Yeah.

00:01:48.413 --> 00:01:49.540
- I wanna, you know,
spend time with my family.

00:01:49.540 --> 00:01:51.380
I wanna spend some time with myself.

00:01:51.380 --> 00:01:52.960
Just kind of get out in
the world and see it."

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:54.900
- It's so good. It's so good for you.

00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:55.949
You're like a walking therapy session.

00:01:55.949 --> 00:01:56.782
It's great.

00:01:56.782 --> 00:01:57.615
(laughs)

00:01:57.615 --> 00:01:59.220
And congrats, I want to say, on your star

00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:00.321
on the walk of fame.

00:02:00.321 --> 00:02:01.154
- Thank you.

00:02:01.154 --> 00:02:01.987
- That's really huge.

00:02:01.987 --> 00:02:02.820
- Yeah, it's-

00:02:02.820 --> 00:02:03.653
- Is that a huge thing for you?

00:02:03.653 --> 00:02:04.670
Like that you dreamed
of since you were a kid?

00:02:04.670 --> 00:02:05.900
- I mean, I think when I was younger,

00:02:05.900 --> 00:02:07.181
I would think about it.

00:02:07.181 --> 00:02:08.014
- Yeah.

00:02:08.014 --> 00:02:08.847
- And you know, you think about,

00:02:08.847 --> 00:02:09.680
"Hey, I want to win an academy award"

00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:10.513
and then you get older and you're like,

00:02:10.513 --> 00:02:12.270
"No, no, no, that's
fine. Let me just work.

00:02:12.270 --> 00:02:13.103
- Yeah.(laughs)

00:02:13.103 --> 00:02:14.690
- I mean do some good works in people.

00:02:14.690 --> 00:02:15.523
- Yeah.

00:02:15.523 --> 00:02:16.863
- And then I realized, you know,

00:02:16.863 --> 00:02:19.240
26 years had gone by and career.

00:02:19.240 --> 00:02:20.750
And I was like, "Oh wow.
I've been here for a while."

00:02:20.750 --> 00:02:22.888
And they presented me with a star,

00:02:22.888 --> 00:02:23.917
- It's so cool.

00:02:23.917 --> 00:02:25.440
- and you know, it's just,
it's there, it's there now.

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:27.640
- Absolutely, with all the other names.

00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:28.473
You walk down there and you're like,

00:02:28.473 --> 00:02:29.980
"Oh my gosh, you're in great company."

00:02:29.980 --> 00:02:30.889
- Yeah.

00:02:30.889 --> 00:02:31.722
- It's amazing.

00:02:31.722 --> 00:02:32.940
- Yeah. A lot of great
people that have them.

00:02:32.940 --> 00:02:35.180
And again, I just, I hope it inspires

00:02:35.180 --> 00:02:36.890
the next generation of like young artists

00:02:36.890 --> 00:02:38.220
and kids and all that to like go out

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:39.560
and do what they want to do.

00:02:39.560 --> 00:02:40.810
- Absolutely. We're lucky.

00:02:40.810 --> 00:02:42.830
I just said that the other day
on the couch with somebody.

00:02:42.830 --> 00:02:44.320
I was like, "We're so lucky."

00:02:44.320 --> 00:02:45.640
They were like saying, "Oh,
you get to do what you love."

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:46.830
I was like, "I know we're so blessed.

00:02:46.830 --> 00:02:48.940
There's so many people
that love to do what we do.

00:02:48.940 --> 00:02:50.820
And we're like the few
that actually got to."

00:02:50.820 --> 00:02:51.801
It's amazing.

00:02:51.801 --> 00:02:52.756
- Yeah, yeah.

00:02:52.756 --> 00:02:54.917
- But, so you started by acting

00:02:54.917 --> 00:02:56.910
and running tech for your
high school production.

00:02:56.910 --> 00:02:57.830
I started in high school,

00:02:57.830 --> 00:02:58.920
like singing and stuff like that.

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:00.210
Was that fun to do the tech stuff?

00:03:00.210 --> 00:03:01.043
- It was a blast.

00:03:01.043 --> 00:03:03.170
I mean, I think it was
a good learning lesson

00:03:03.170 --> 00:03:05.870
to, you know, not just be on
stage and in front of people,

00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:08.420
but it was like, "Hey, how's
the entirety production happen?

00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:09.253
- Yeah.

00:03:09.253 --> 00:03:10.086
- So, I mean, when I was a kid,

00:03:10.086 --> 00:03:11.010
I had a truck in high school.

00:03:11.010 --> 00:03:13.810
And so my high school drama
teacher, Mariana Herrero,

00:03:13.810 --> 00:03:14.643
she would be like,

00:03:14.643 --> 00:03:17.347
"Hey, you're in charge of
going to Hollywood to pick."

00:03:17.347 --> 00:03:18.310
"Cause I grew up in Orange County-

00:03:18.310 --> 00:03:19.560
- Oh and you're the guy with the truck.

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:20.393
- I'm the guy with the ruck,

00:03:20.393 --> 00:03:22.040
so I'd go pick up the
lights, pick up sets,

00:03:22.040 --> 00:03:23.560
pick up lumber, pick up all this stuff

00:03:23.560 --> 00:03:26.830
and build sets and hang
lights and sew costumes.

00:03:26.830 --> 00:03:28.780
And I kind of continued that
through college too, so.

00:03:28.780 --> 00:03:30.950
- I think that's amazing,
'cause you're well-rounded.

00:03:30.950 --> 00:03:32.460
And also I think that sometimes people

00:03:32.460 --> 00:03:34.730
don't respect everybody's job on set,

00:03:34.730 --> 00:03:35.827
because you don't know what it's like

00:03:35.827 --> 00:03:37.530
and it might seem easy to you.

00:03:37.530 --> 00:03:39.730
I think that that's really
well-rounded of you,

00:03:39.730 --> 00:03:40.910
because you're on set and you know

00:03:40.910 --> 00:03:42.700
that kind of what everyone's doing.

00:03:42.700 --> 00:03:43.830
And you've been in there a little bit.

00:03:43.830 --> 00:03:44.768
I think that's important.

00:03:44.768 --> 00:03:46.120
- You understand but at the
same time it's like, why,

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:47.770
like we should all just
respect each other's jobs

00:03:47.770 --> 00:03:48.603
to begin with.

00:03:48.603 --> 00:03:49.730
- Totally, but it's a different thing.

00:03:49.730 --> 00:03:51.040
It's like, have you
ever gone out to dinner

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:52.460
with somebody who's never waited tables?

00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:53.293
- Absolutely.

00:03:53.293 --> 00:03:54.523
- Yeah and you're like, "Okay."

00:03:54.523 --> 00:03:55.356
- And they're not looking
the waiter in the eye.

00:03:55.356 --> 00:03:56.920
Like, "Oh yeah, I'll take this, whatever."

00:03:56.920 --> 00:03:57.753
- Yeah.

00:03:57.753 --> 00:03:59.196
And it's like, just stop,

00:03:59.196 --> 00:04:00.380
look them in the eye,
say please and thank you.

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:01.470
- And there's other tables.

00:04:01.470 --> 00:04:03.200
It's not just you that
came in to eat tonight.

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:04.033
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:04:04.033 --> 00:04:05.368
- It's so fun to do that.

00:04:05.368 --> 00:04:06.760
'Cause I was a waitress.

00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:08.386
- So was I. I waited tables too.

00:04:08.386 --> 00:04:09.637
Yeah and it's like,

00:04:09.637 --> 00:04:10.480
I feel like every like actor, musician

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:11.410
has waited tables.

00:04:11.410 --> 00:04:12.760
- Yeah. You have to, you have to have had,

00:04:12.760 --> 00:04:14.180
because it's a nighttime job.

00:04:14.180 --> 00:04:15.363
So you got daytime to do your stuff.

00:04:15.363 --> 00:04:17.120
- Exactly and you can change your hours.

00:04:17.120 --> 00:04:18.150
- Change your hours, yeah.

00:04:18.150 --> 00:04:19.780
You're always like swapping
shifts and whatnot.

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:20.613
- You get it.

00:04:20.613 --> 00:04:21.446
- I totally get it.

00:04:21.446 --> 00:04:23.570
- But wait, I also heard that
you're learning Japanese.

00:04:23.570 --> 00:04:24.910
So one, like why?

00:04:24.910 --> 00:04:26.920
like that's so, it's such a random thing

00:04:26.920 --> 00:04:28.040
to want to learn.

00:04:28.040 --> 00:04:30.320
- I kind of needed to do
something different with my brain.

00:04:30.320 --> 00:04:32.490
Cause like, you know, you
settle into what we do

00:04:32.490 --> 00:04:33.500
and like great.

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:36.560
I learn my lines, I show
up I'm Mo, I'm an actor.

00:04:36.560 --> 00:04:39.220
Point the camera wherever.
Great, I'm directing,

00:04:39.220 --> 00:04:41.320
I'm putting projects together,
working with writers.

00:04:41.320 --> 00:04:42.800
Great I'm producing.

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:44.790
I needed to do something else with my head

00:04:44.790 --> 00:04:46.910
just to keep active, to keep learning,

00:04:46.910 --> 00:04:48.230
to kinda keep growing.

00:04:48.230 --> 00:04:49.115
And I was like-
- Breaks up the monotony.

00:04:49.115 --> 00:04:49.948
- It does. It absolutely does.

00:04:49.948 --> 00:04:51.476
But then this is, you know,

00:04:51.476 --> 00:04:54.120
a few years ago I haven't
been up to date on it as much,

00:04:54.120 --> 00:04:57.030
but like I started
learning Russian, Spanish,

00:04:57.030 --> 00:04:58.519
and Japanese at the same time.

00:04:58.519 --> 00:04:59.352
- What?

00:04:59.352 --> 00:05:00.185
- Realized it was too ambitious

00:05:00.185 --> 00:05:01.580
with my work schedule on "This is Us."

00:05:01.580 --> 00:05:03.220
So I just backed off on Japanese.

00:05:03.220 --> 00:05:05.810
And now I haven't been in class like

00:05:05.810 --> 00:05:07.050
with my teacher in a while,

00:05:07.050 --> 00:05:09.390
but like it's floating
around in there somewhere.

00:05:09.390 --> 00:05:11.340
- Yeah, that's why I love my kids.

00:05:11.340 --> 00:05:13.210
And so I went to a school where there,

00:05:13.210 --> 00:05:14.420
you could learn Spanish. That was it.

00:05:14.420 --> 00:05:16.010
That was your option basically.

00:05:16.010 --> 00:05:18.680
And it's cool, cause now
they have all these options

00:05:18.680 --> 00:05:20.256
and it's so good when
you're a kid to learn.

00:05:20.256 --> 00:05:21.089
- Oh yeah.

00:05:21.089 --> 00:05:22.047
- Like, you know, 'cause when
you're older, it's harder.

00:05:22.047 --> 00:05:23.794
- It's hard, yeah, when
you're in your forties yeah.

00:05:23.794 --> 00:05:24.740
'Cause I have like every language

00:05:24.740 --> 00:05:26.221
from Rosetta Stone in my house.

00:05:26.221 --> 00:05:27.215
(laughs)

00:05:27.215 --> 00:05:28.779
'Cause I'm like, yeah,
I'm gonna do it this year.

00:05:28.779 --> 00:05:29.612
And then I'm, I know a
bit of Spanish, that's it.

00:05:29.612 --> 00:05:30.850
And French.
- I've done Rosetta Stone,

00:05:30.850 --> 00:05:32.038
I've done all those sayings.

00:05:32.038 --> 00:05:33.979
- Oh, Duolingo that owl
is so disappointed in me.

00:05:33.979 --> 00:05:35.078
(laughs)

00:05:35.078 --> 00:05:35.925
- Yeah, totally.

00:05:35.925 --> 00:05:37.890
- I'm like, "Look owl, I'm a
momma too with a lot of jobs."

00:05:37.890 --> 00:05:38.940
- Yeah, totally.

00:05:38.940 --> 00:05:40.360
- But anyway, I want to say,

00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:42.330
do you have like a
favorite phrase in Japanese

00:05:42.330 --> 00:05:43.163
that you've learned?

00:05:43.163 --> 00:05:44.260
- You know there's, what I loved

00:05:44.260 --> 00:05:46.470
about the Japanese language is,

00:05:46.470 --> 00:05:48.920
you know, it's not just
word represents this,

00:05:48.920 --> 00:05:51.499
but they'll have a word
that would represent

00:05:51.499 --> 00:05:52.966
kind of an experience.

00:05:52.966 --> 00:05:53.799
- Oh.

00:05:53.799 --> 00:05:56.010
- Like there's this one word
it's, (foreign language),

00:05:56.010 --> 00:05:59.220
which is the way that light,

00:05:59.220 --> 00:06:01.700
specifically I think the sun,

00:06:01.700 --> 00:06:05.600
travels through a tree and
makes a shadow on the ground.

00:06:05.600 --> 00:06:06.433
- That's won-

00:06:06.433 --> 00:06:07.266
- But it's like,

00:06:07.266 --> 00:06:08.870
It's a whole expanded experience with it

00:06:08.870 --> 00:06:11.010
besides just being a word

00:06:11.010 --> 00:06:12.940
that you can use to describe something.

00:06:12.940 --> 00:06:13.773
- Wow.

00:06:13.773 --> 00:06:14.705
- Yeah.

00:06:14.705 --> 00:06:15.538
- That's beautiful.

00:06:15.538 --> 00:06:16.500
- I don't really have a lot of opportunity

00:06:16.500 --> 00:06:18.207
to talk about ( foreign language),

00:06:18.207 --> 00:06:19.828
but like that's a really nice word.

00:06:19.828 --> 00:06:20.920
- But it's cool that
it exists. I love that.

00:06:20.920 --> 00:06:22.630
And like different
languages that they're like,

00:06:22.630 --> 00:06:24.010
you don't have a word
for it, but it's this.

00:06:24.010 --> 00:06:25.100
And I'm like, "That's beautiful.

00:06:25.100 --> 00:06:26.610
Why don't we get a word for it?"

00:06:26.610 --> 00:06:28.131
We're such a confusing
language in general.

00:06:28.131 --> 00:06:28.964
- Yeah.

00:06:28.964 --> 00:06:29.937
- Like we couldn't do that as well.

00:06:29.937 --> 00:06:33.340
So everybody is sad that "This
is Us" is coming to an end.

00:06:33.340 --> 00:06:35.220
So are you feeling kind
of bittersweet about it?

00:06:35.220 --> 00:06:36.300
Like it's a great cast,

00:06:36.300 --> 00:06:37.890
but are you excited
about doing new things?

00:06:37.890 --> 00:06:39.680
- I mean, you know, look,
I'll be honest for me.

00:06:39.680 --> 00:06:40.790
I mean, I don't really work with anybody,

00:06:40.790 --> 00:06:43.433
but Mandy 'cause I'm, you know,
deceased in the present day.

00:06:43.433 --> 00:06:44.266
- Oh, that's true, that's true.

00:06:44.266 --> 00:06:45.099
- I never worked with the kids.

00:06:45.099 --> 00:06:46.110
